<body>

  <%- include("partials/tool-header") %>

  <main class="info-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="section-eyebrow">FILEVORA</div>

        <h1>Security</h1>

        <p class="info-lead">
          How FileVora approaches file processing, website security and safer
          use of online tools.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-date">
          Last updated: September 20, 2026
        </p>

        <div class="legal-content">
          <div class="security-note">
            <strong>Important security reminder</strong>
            Avoid processing confidential, highly sensitive or irreplaceable
            information through any online service unless you understand and
            accept how that service handles your data.
          </div>

          <h2>1. Browser-Based Processing</h2>

          <p>
            FileVora is designed so that many tools process files, text and
            calculations directly inside your browser. When a tool operates
            locally, the selected file remains on your device and is not
            intentionally uploaded to FileVora’s servers.
          </p>

          <p>
            Processing behaviour may differ according to the selected tool,
            browser, device, third-party libraries and future service updates.
            You should review the operation of a tool before using it with
            sensitive information.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Secure Website Connection</h2>

          <p>
            FileVora is delivered through HTTPS, which helps protect data
            transmitted between your browser and the website from interception
            while in transit.
          </p>

          <p>
            HTTPS improves connection security, but it cannot protect against
            every threat, such as compromised devices, unsafe browser
            extensions, malware or files obtained from untrusted sources.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Hosting and Infrastructure</h2>

          <p>
            FileVora relies on third-party hosting, content delivery and
            infrastructure providers to deliver and protect the website. These
            providers may use their own technical and organizational security
            measures.
          </p>

          <p>
            Limited technical logs may be generated by hosting or security
            systems for reliability, diagnostics, abuse prevention and
            protection of the service.
          </p>

          <h2>4. No Permanent File Storage</h2>

          <p>
            FileVora is not a cloud storage or file backup service. Files
            processed locally by browser-based tools are not intentionally
            stored by FileVora.
          </p>

          <p>
            You should save your results promptly and retain secure backup
            copies of all important original files.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Third-Party Libraries and Services</h2>

          <p>
            Some FileVora features may depend on third-party JavaScript
            libraries, APIs, hosting services, advertisements or content
            delivery networks.
          </p>

          <p>
            Third-party services operate under their own terms, security
            practices and privacy policies. FileVora cannot guarantee the
            security or availability of services that it does not control.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Your Security Responsibilities</h2>

          <p>
            You can reduce security risks by following these practices:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>Keep your browser and operating system updated</li>
            <li>Use trusted antivirus and security software</li>
            <li>Avoid processing unknown or suspicious files</li>
            <li>Do not disable browser security warnings</li>
            <li>Use secure networks when accessing online services</li>
            <li>Keep backups of important original files</li>
            <li>Review generated or converted files before opening or sharing them</li>
            <li>Avoid entering passwords or private keys into unrelated tools</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>7. Sensitive Information</h2>

          <p>
            Do not use FileVora to process information such as account
            passwords, payment card details, private encryption keys, medical
            records, government identification documents or other highly
            sensitive personal information unless you have carefully reviewed
            the relevant tool and understand the risks.
          </p>

          <h2>8. File Safety</h2>

          <p>
            FileVora does not guarantee that every file selected by a user is
            safe. You are responsible for checking files obtained from external
            sources before processing, opening or sharing them.
          </p>

          <p>
            A converted or modified file may still contain harmful, misleading
            or unauthorized content. File conversion should not be treated as a
            malware removal or security-scanning service.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Security Limitations</h2>

          <p>
            No website, browser application, network or electronic storage
            system can be guaranteed to be completely secure. FileVora cannot
            guarantee protection from every vulnerability, attack, service
            interruption or unauthorized third-party action.
          </p>

          <p>
            Use of FileVora is subject to our
            <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and
            <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Reporting a Security Concern</h2>

          <p>
            If you believe you have discovered a security issue affecting
            FileVora, please report it responsibly through our
            <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            Include a clear description of the issue and the affected page or
            tool. Do not publicly disclose a potential vulnerability or access
            data that does not belong to you.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Privacy</h2>

          <p>
            For information about technical data, cookies, advertising and
            third-party services, please read our
            <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>12. Changes to This Security Page</h2>

          <p>
            We may update this page when FileVora’s tools, infrastructure or
            security practices change. Updates will appear here with a revised
            “Last updated” date.
          </p>
        </div>

